9. Explain how MongoDB can be used for event logging. Design a suitable document structure for storing application or system events.
MongoDB is excellent for event logging because of high write throughput, flexible schema, and TTL indexes.
Suggested document structure:
{
  _id: ObjectId("..."),
  timestamp: ISODate("2026-10-12T10:30:00Z"),
  level: "ERROR",                    // INFO, WARN, ERROR, DEBUG
  service: "payment-service",
  eventType: "payment_failed",
  userId: "user_12345",
  sessionId: "sess_abc",
  message: "Payment gateway timeout",
  metadata: {
    amount: 1500,
    currency: "INR",
    gateway: "Razorpay",
    ip: "192.168.1.10"
  },
  stackTrace: "...",                 // optional
  tags: ["payment", "critical"]
}
Useful features: TTL index on timestamp for automatic deletion of old logs, time-series collections (MongoDB 5.0+), and aggregation for analytics.
